Z||000011||gtsuzi||04-03-2001||09:11 PM||||Never expected to recieve so many welcomes!<BR>Thanks so much to everyone!<BR>My car is a gold tone 86 6 cyl standard transmission GT and I love it.  It has been in our family since purchased new in '86.  It is garaged kept and is still in excellent condition.  Only has 52000 miles and runs perfect.<BR>Hope I don't sound like I am bragging, but well I guess I am.<BR>Looking forward to future chats with everyone.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cheever2||04-03-2001||10:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Hope I don't sound like I am bragging, but well I guess I am.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>That's the 1st Commandment in car forums: "He who tooteth not his own horn, it is he whose horn shall not be tooted".<P>Besides, around here it's not considered "your" Fiero, it's "our" Fiero.  I'm j/k really, but let's continue:  We're a brotherhood/sisterhood, and we are all equally responsible for whatever needs to be done to keep all Fieros alive.  Anything and everything must be done to keep a Fiero from going to the salvage yard, but when it must be, then its organs -er, parts- are donated to the emergency maintenance of other needy Fieros, and we all bid fond farewell to those who sacrificed so much for so few.  So, when you're one of us -and you are now, there's no turning back- not only do you get our unending concern for the best care your Fiero can receive, but you in turn have a responsibility to reciprocate.  You ask "What can <I>I</I> do?", well first you can learn how to post pics of your car here, and do it often.  Secondly, you can share any experiences you have which may benefit us, such as kill stories and overcoming maintenance difficulties.  Third, you can laugh at our sick jokes and provide some humor of your own.  Fourth, ask something once in a while which we are able to answer, so we can justify to our significant others what good we have done by staring at these shades of blue screens for so long.  As you grow in your post count, and in your understanding of the Search feature, you will attain the glow of pride which is a part of being a Forum member!  For that is the meaning of the word Fiero: Pride, and the greatest benefit of being one of us.<P>Just stay away from Stimpy.<P>j/k<P><BR>||||reg||6
